WEBVTT

00:03.920 --> 00:04.320
All right.

00:04.320 --> 00:05.840
So now moving on to the next one.

00:06.120 --> 00:10.160
As we learned, identifying an unused index is an important task.

00:10.360 --> 00:17.520
But in the other hand identifying a missing index is as well very important to improve the performance

00:17.520 --> 00:18.440
of your queries.

00:18.560 --> 00:25.160
So in SQL server you can get recommendations from the database itself about missing indexes for your

00:25.160 --> 00:25.680
query.

00:25.800 --> 00:28.240
So let's see where we can find those recommendations.

00:28.280 --> 00:28.640
All right.

00:28.640 --> 00:33.160
So now let's say that you are doing multiple queries and you are doing analysis and so on.

00:33.160 --> 00:35.280
For example I have this query over here.

00:35.280 --> 00:38.080
It is query on the database Adventureworks DW.

00:38.280 --> 00:40.280
And I'm joining just two tables.

00:40.280 --> 00:47.000
The fact with the dimension and then filtering the data based on the colors and as well on the datekey

00:47.040 --> 00:48.960
where I have like a range over here.

00:48.960 --> 00:52.080
So once I executed I got the following informations.

00:52.080 --> 00:55.840
It could be any query that you are doing while practicing and analyzing and so on.

00:55.840 --> 01:01.200
So now if you have like slow query and so on, you can go and check the recommendations from the database

01:01.200 --> 01:02.760
about missing indexes.

01:02.760 --> 01:08.990
So in order to do that we can go and check again the metadata from the database system to see the recommendations

01:08.990 --> 01:10.190
about the missing indexes.

01:10.190 --> 01:11.230
So let's go and do that.

01:11.230 --> 01:13.230
So we're going to go and select from.

01:13.270 --> 01:16.510
And now we have to go and target the dynamic management views.

01:16.550 --> 01:24.390
And it is like this DM underscore db underscore missing index details.

01:24.550 --> 01:27.630
So let's go and explore that content over here.

01:27.630 --> 01:32.230
And don't forget that those informations are going to be inside the cache of the server.

01:32.230 --> 01:36.870
And if there's like a restart or something on the server you will lose all those informations.

01:36.870 --> 01:41.350
So now from my query there is few suggestions and recommendations from the database.

01:41.350 --> 01:46.790
Let's go and check it so we can see here there are four recommendations about missing indexes from the

01:46.790 --> 01:47.550
database.

01:47.550 --> 01:49.750
So now let's go and check the first recommendation.

01:49.750 --> 01:50.510
Over here.

01:50.510 --> 01:53.230
You can go and check the table name from the object ID.

01:53.230 --> 01:55.270
Or you can find it here in the statements.

01:55.270 --> 01:59.950
So here the database is suggesting an index for the table dimension products.

01:59.950 --> 02:03.670
And it is recommending us to make an index for the column color.

02:03.670 --> 02:07.870
And that's because if you check our query we have like here a filter the where condition where we are

02:07.870 --> 02:09.670
seeing the color equal to black.

02:09.670 --> 02:15.130
And since we don't have an index on the color scale, is just suggesting to use an index for the color.

02:15.130 --> 02:18.450
And of course, in this situation we can go and use a non-clustered index.

02:18.450 --> 02:23.970
Now after that we have three recommendations for the same table fact internet sales.

02:23.970 --> 02:29.490
So for example here it is suggesting to make an index on the order date key because we are using it

02:29.490 --> 02:30.850
in the filter over here.

02:30.850 --> 02:36.490
And as well suggesting to make an index for the product key since we are using it for the join.

02:36.490 --> 02:40.730
So this is really nice report about missing indexes in the database.

02:40.730 --> 02:44.730
And it could assist you to find out things that you didn't thought about.

02:44.730 --> 02:49.170
But here my recommendation is evaluate those informations very carefully.

02:49.170 --> 02:53.370
Don't go and create like an index for each suggestions from the database.

02:53.370 --> 02:54.810
You still have to think about it.

02:54.850 --> 02:56.330
Is it really necessary?

02:56.450 --> 02:59.930
Do we really use this query very frequently and so on.

02:59.930 --> 03:04.490
So don't go blindly creating indexes for each recommendations from the database.

03:04.490 --> 03:10.130
So this is really nice tool and assistant for you in order to make a good strategy for your indexing.

03:10.130 --> 03:15.290
So this is how you find the recommendations of missing indexes from SQL database.
